      "description": {
        "fun": "Despite the name, Sandshrew is more armadillo or pangolin than shrew: it curls into a tight ball to survive falls and attacks, and spends most of its time in deep burrows. Its dry hide soaks up water efficiently, which suits desert life, but if it gets too wet its skin goes wrinkly and it has to dry off near a volcano or with a sand bath.",
